{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If his offering is an olah.</b> When he volunteers in this language, Scripture begins with the olah because it is superior and goes up entirely upward." "<b>He shall offer it.</b> He shall consecrate it, and say: this I have consecrated to the Most High." "<b>To the entrance of the Tent of Meeting he shall bring it.</b> That the offerer should not say to the priest: go and take the animal in my house that I volunteered and make it an offering — for this is not a way of honoring the One above." "<b>To his acceptance.</b> Since this is a freewill offering, לרצונו is stated regarding it; but regarding other offerings לרצונו is not written, since sometimes they come as an obligation." "<b>Before HaShem and lay his hand.</b> Even though he laid his hand outside, he must return and lay his hand inside."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:34.103606791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}